  "question": {
    "text": "A heavy, flexible uniform chain of length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi><mi>r</mi></math> and mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>λ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo></math>lies in a smooth semicircular tube <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>AB</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo></math>of the radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math>. Assuming a slight disturbance to start the chain in motion, find the velocity&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi></math> with which it will emerge from the end&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> of the tube.<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/EM0014750_Question_1_1.jpg\" style=\"width: 249px; height: 164px;\" />",
    "image": null
  },
